				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/monteparnas" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2926286); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2926286&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608930995" alt="Monteparnas" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2926286)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/monteparnas" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2926286); return false;" >Monteparnas</a></span> <span class="odate time_1541645846 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">08 Nov 2018 02:57</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4052939">
									

<p>I loved the AWCY? proposal and upvoted it. It was very good even on its own.</p>
<p>Also, I upvoted the KTE main article because it was good enough and served as the basis for both the AWCY? and this one, though it wasn't that great by itself.</p>
<p>But I just had to downvote this one. The concept is very good, and it had some great moments, but there are several problems down the road. The tone seems forced most of the time, the narrative drags frequently, main characters are too shallow behind unnecessary colorful description. I started to cringe with the opening scene, where light works just wrong (y'know, when the sun rises, light comes from above, not below), and it didn't get as better as I wished.</p>
<p>The core story, though, needs just a few tweaks to be really great, so I will keep an eye here to change my vote as soon as it achieves enough of my expectations. I want this tale to work, really do.</p>

							</div>

								
					
